  description="Familial glucocorticoid deficiency is inherited cortisol failure with ACTH running high. The classic causes are a broken MC2R, or a broken MRAP so the receptor never reaches the cell surface. Aldosterone is usually spared. The skin darkens because the unused ACTH spills onto MC1R. There is no drug that repairs the receptor; treatment is cortisol replacement."
